expected_legal_description:
ALL THAT CERTAIN tract or parcel of land and premises situate, lying and being in the Borough of HADDONFIELD, County of CAMDEN and State of New Jersey more particularly described as follows:

BEGINNING at a point in the Southeasterly line of Kings Highway East, as approved December 15, 1931 and adopted by Ordinance February 16, 1932 by Borough Commissioners, 171.76 feet Northeastwardly from the Easterly corner of Kings Highway East and Chestnut Street, said beginning point being corner to remaining lands of George W, Westcoatt and Dorothy F. Westcoatt;

THENCE:  Northeastwardly along Southeasterly line of Kings Highway East, 84 feet to point corner to lands of Trustees of Baptist Church of Haddonfield (formerly John Clement) and said point also being 97.23 feet Southwestwardly from foundation wall of 128 Kings Highway East (Hunt's cellar wall);

THENCE:  Southeastwardly forming interior angles of 89 degrees 46 minutes 45 seconds with Kings Highway East and running along lands of said Trustees of Baptist Church of Haddonfield 231.84 feet to point in line of said Trustees of Baptist Church and corner to lands of the Borough of Haddonfield;

THENCE:  Southwestwardly along lands of Borough of Haddonfield and forming an interior angle of 89 degrees 44 minutes 10 seconds with the last course 83.05 feet to point corner of remaining lands of Estate of Charles H. Ellis;

THENCE:  Northwestwardly along line of remaining land of Estate of Charles H. Ellis and also along line of remaining lands of George W. Westcoatt and Dorothy F. Westcoatt aforesaid and forming an interior angle of 90 degrees 30 minutes with last course and also forming an interior angle of 89 degrees 59 minutes 5 seconds with Kings Highway East 231.15 feet to Southeasterly line of Kings Highway East and place of Beginning.

BEING KNOWN as Lot 6, Block 34, as shown on the tax map of the Borough of Haddonfield.  (For information only)

